1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,947
You clap once.

2
00:00:00,947 --> 00:00:02,697
The applause
keeps arriving.

3
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:05,600
Eight point three
billion people.

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,980
Sixteen point six
billion hands.

5
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:09,510
All meeting
at once.

6
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:13,060
Each clap squeezes
air into a pulse.

7
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:14,220
Your own
clap reaches

8
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:15,590
your ears first.

9
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:18,160
Follow that
same pulse

10
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,740
for a kilometer.

11
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:21,060
It takes
almost three

12
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:22,670
seconds to
get there.

13
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:24,700
Everyone stops
together.

14
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:25,760
Where you stand

15
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:27,610
changes what
you hear.

16
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,020
Without reflections,

17
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:31,620
doubling the
distance drops an

18
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:34,430
isolated clap about
six decibels.

19
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,700
Nearby walls bounce
some sound back.

20
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:38,980
You hear
a reply.

21
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,470
Nobody clapped
again.

22
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:43,820
A global
clap becomes

23
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:45,310
local applause.

24
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:47,970
Your encore comes
from a wall.
